# Power BI Day 3 – Laptop Data Transformation & Business Analysis

## Dataset

Laptop dataset containing laptop specifications,
memory, processor, GPU, operating system, weight and price.

## Tool

Power BI – Power Query

## Topics Practiced

- Conditional Columns
- Custom Columns
- Text Extraction
- Numeric Calculations
- Data Categorization
- Data Validation
- Business Rules
- Data Quality Checks

## Business Transformation

Created analytical categories to make the dataset easier
to analyze in Power BI.

### Price Analysis

Created `Price_Category` to classify laptops into:

- Budget
- Mid Range
- Premium
- High End

### RAM Analysis

Created `RAM_Category` to classify laptops based on RAM:

- Basic
- Standard
- High
- Very High

### Weight Analysis

Created `Weight_Category`:

- Lightweight
- Standard
- Heavy
- Very Heavy

### Screen Resolution Analysis

Created:

- Screen_Width
- Screen_Height

from the original Screen_Resolution column.


### RAM Conversion

Created:

- Total_RAM_MB

by converting RAM from GB to MB.

## Data Validation

Validated:

- Missing values
- Data types
- Text consistency
- Numeric columns
- Error values
- Derived columns

## Learning Outcome

Learned how to transform cleaned data into
analysis-ready business categories using Power Query.
